"""al — generate an agentic layer for any codebase.

  al init    APP [--layer DIR]     create the layer directory beside the app and scout a draft LLM.txt
  al init    APP --in-repo [--dir agentic]   … or inside the application repository, committed with it
  al scout   APP [-o LLM.txt]      deterministic LLM.txt draft (an LLM completes it: meta/commands/scout-codebase.md)
  al compile LAYER                 agentic.rkt -> agentic-layer.json (validated against the schema)
  al gen     LAYER [--discard-edits]  compile + generate commands, HOPs, ADWs, env, triggers, forge files
  al explain LAYER [--md F] [--gif F]  explain the layer definition in plain language, block by block
  al check   LAYER                 verify a generated layer and that the application tree is untouched
  al eject   LAYER (command|hop|expert) NAME [--force] | --list
                                   copy a kit template into LAYER/templates/ so your edits to it survive `al gen`
  al improve LAYER "request" [--dry-run] [--review human|agent] [--model-set T] [--model T=ID] [--max-cost USD]
                                   change the layer through al's own reviewed workflow: ends in a pull request
  al adopt   LAYER [--app APP] [--dry-run] [--only rules|prompts|workflows …]
                                   bring a codebase's existing agent setup (rule files, prompts, workflow
                                   scripts) into the layer, deterministically; reports what a person must decide
  al dashboard [LAYER_OR_DIR …] [--port N] [--open] [--podman]
                                   watch the runs of any layers (or every layer below a directory) live, read-only
  al verify  LAYER [--cmd NAME …] [--timeout S] [--json]
                                   run the layer's codebase cmds on a throwaway worktree, in the ADWs' environment

LAYER is the directory holding agentic.rkt. Nothing is ever written into APP, except with `al init APP --in-repo`,
which puts the layer (a directory that is committed with the code) inside the application repository.
"""
